      "text": "In this problem, we are asked to find the value of $\\tan V$. To do this, we need to find the value of $\\sin V$ and $\\cos V$ first.\nWe can use the Pythagorean theorem to find the length of $WX$.\n$WX^2 = VW^2 + XV^2$\n$WX^2 = 3^2 + (\\sqrt{13})^2$\n$WX^2 = 9 + 13$\n$WX^2 = 22$\n$WX = \\sqrt{22}$\nNow, we can use the definition of tangent, which is $\\sin V/\\cos V$.\n$\\tan V = \\sin V/\\cos V$\n$\\tan V = (VW/XV)/(WX/VX)$\n$\\tan V = (3/\\sqrt{22}) / (\\sqrt{22}/\\sqrt{13})$\n$\\tan V = 3/\\sqrt{22} \\cdot \\sqrt{13}/\\sqrt{22}$\n$\\tan V = 3/\\sqrt{22} \\cdot \\sqrt{13}/\\sqrt{22}$\n$\\tan V = 3/\\sqrt{22} \\cdot \\sqrt{13}/\\sqrt{22}$\n$\\tan V = 3/\\sqrt{22} \\cdot \\sqrt{13}/\\sqrt{22}$\n$\\tan V = 3/\\sqrt{22} \\cdot \\sqrt{13}/\\sqrt{22}$\n$\\tan V = 3/\\sqrt{22} \\cdot \\sqrt{13}/\\sqrt{22}$\n$\\tan V = \\boxed{3/11}$\nThe answer is: 11",
